#### Step 2: Sequential Skill Audits (One by One)
Run three distinct, thorough audit passes across all discovered files:

- **Pass 1 — `compose-expert` Audit:**
  - Load `compose-expert` first and evaluate every relevant file against its guidelines.
  - Check Compose architecture, Unidirectional Data Flow (UDF), state hoisting, ViewModel/UI-state boundaries, side-effect APIs (`LaunchedEffect`, `DisposableEffect`, `SideEffect`, `rememberCoroutineScope`), lifecycle awareness (`collectAsStateWithLifecycle`), Modifier ordering & chaining, slot APIs, composable scoping/reusability, navigation patterns, and `@Preview` coverage.

- **Pass 2 — `jetpack-compose-performance` Audit:**
  - Load `jetpack-compose-performance` second and re-evaluate every relevant file strictly for runtime and composition performance.
  - Check recomposition scopes, parameter stability (`@Immutable`, `@Stable`, unstable collections/lambdas, kotlinx-collections-immutable or strong skipping implications), improper `remember` / `derivedStateOf` usage, reading state too high in the tree (instead of deferring via lambdas or `Modifier.offset { }` / `drawBehind`), `LazyColumn`/`LazyRow`/`LazyVerticalGrid` missing `key` and `contentType`, heavy allocations or side effects inside composition, and unnecessary layout passes/subcomposition.

- **Pass 3 — `material-design-3-ui` Audit:**
  - Load `material-design-3-ui` third and re-evaluate all UI, theme, and resource files strictly for Material Design 3 compliance and UX quality.
  - Check `MaterialTheme` setup (ColorScheme, dynamic color, Typography scale, Shapes), hardcoded colors/dimensions instead of theme tokens, proper M3 components vs. legacy M2 or custom hacks, dark/light theme parity, edge-to-edge & `WindowInsets` handling, spacing/alignment consistency, touch target sizes (minimum 48dp), contrast, and accessibility (`contentDescription`, semantics, role descriptions).

